##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# Multi-threaded tile-fetch stress scene targeting CSynthesizedTileSource
# specifically, spec 020 (020-runtime-tile-paging) T024. Mirrors spec 019's
# own concurrency-scene.rib exactly (large, frontal, periodically-wrapped
# polygon, diced at a fine ShadingRate so many micropolygon grids --
# processed across many REYES buckets, hence many threads -- fault in many
# distinct tiles concurrently; periodic wrap makes multiple buckets/threads
# race to fault in the SAME early tile too, not just distinct ones), but
# referencing large_rgb8.png (spec 018's fixture, tests/unit/image_input/
# fixtures/) DIRECTLY -- no otexmake bake step, no disk cache (this scene
# deliberately has no "Option \"texturecache\"" statement, so the cache
# stays at its default-disabled state) -- so CRenderer::textureLoad()'s
# fallback always goes through CSynthesizedTileSource, not CTiffTileSource,
# which is what spec 019's own concurrency-scene.rib already exercises and
# is therefore not this test's concern.
version 3.03
Hider "reyes"
Display "synthesized-concurrency-scene.tif" "file" "rgba"
Projection "orthographic"
ShadingRate 0.25
Translate 0 0 4
Surface "paintedplastic" "texturename" ["large_rgb8.png"]
WorldBegin
  LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [1]
  Patch "bilinear" "P" [-4 -4 0  4 -4 0  -4 4 0  4 4 0]
        "st" [0 0  8 0  0 8  8 8]
WorldEnd
